  "actions": [
    {
      "name": "show_moment",
      "description": "Show and narrate one moment with the lesson’s own words, then continue this turn into something for the child to notice, answer or do. Some moments are help on the work in hand: it is kept, and recorded as helped. Others replace what is on screen, so they are refused while a question is unanswered. rainbow_scene: the opening meadow, Sun behind Mia, rain ahead, rainbow in her window. sunlight_path: HELP on the CURRENT outdoor setup; draws sunlight arrows and any coloured light coming back to Mia, and says why she does or does not see a rainbow. inside_drop: close-up of one drop, light bends in, bounces off the back, bends out on the Sun’s side; use when the child wonders what the drops do. Pauses current work without losing it; resume_activity returns to it. colours_spread: the same close-up, white sunlight fans into colours that were already in it; use for \"where do the colours come from\" or \"the water makes the colours\". Pauses current work without losing it. why_a_bow: deeper, only once Sun-behind and the drop are familiar: the drops that send colour form a circle round the line from Sun through head to shadow. red_on_top: deeper: higher drops send red, lower send violet. high_sun: deeper: midday Sun, bow below the ground.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "moment": {
            "enum": [
              "rainbow_scene",
              "sunlight_path",
              "inside_drop",
              "colours_spread",
              "why_a_bow",
              "red_on_top",
              "high_sun"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "moment"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "start_activity",
      "description": "Hand the child something to do on the scene; the lesson speaks the instruction. Unanswered work must be answered or left first. sun_and_rain: unscored investigation: tap the clouds; a rainbow needs sunlight AND drops. turn_to_find: unscored investigation: turn Mia; she must face away from the Sun. walk_around: unscored investigation: walk Mia round the shower while she faces it; she must stand with the Sun behind her. make_rainbow: transfer, harder: a fountain, Sun on the other side, everything free; the child builds the rainbow. Reaching it unaided counts as evidence. aim_sunbeam: unscored investigation in the drop close-up: slide the beam and see the colours always leave on the Sun’s side. sun_height: deeper, unscored: lift the Sun and watch the bow sink.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "activity": {
            "enum": [
              "sun_and_rain",
              "turn_to_find",
              "walk_around",
              "make_rainbow",
              "aim_sunbeam",
              "sun_height"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "activity"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "start_check",
      "description": "Ask one question; the lesson speaks the exact words shown on screen. Wait for the answer and do not ask another. see_rainbow: needs a situation, shown with sunlight arrows kept and Mia’s window covered: sun_behind (yes), far_side, side_on, facing_sun, cloud_over_sun, water_off, high_sun (all no; high_sun only after that moment). With fresh it is transfer: a new arrangement with no arrows; repeat for more practice at the same demand. sun_where: where should the Sun be (behind / in front). drop_exit: in the close-up, where the light comes out after the bounce. drop_colours: whether the colours were in the sunlight or made by the drop. reach_rainbow: deeper: can Mia walk to the rainbow. Situations: see_rainbow takes sun_behind, far_side, side_on, facing_sun, cloud_over_sun, water_off, high_sun, fresh (a new arrangement each time).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "question": {
            "enum": [
              "see_rainbow",
              "sun_where",
              "drop_exit",
              "drop_colours",
              "reach_rainbow"
            ]
          },
          "situation": {
            "enum": [
              "sun_behind",
              "far_side",
              "side_on",
              "facing_sun",
              "cloud_over_sun",
              "water_off",
              "high_sun",
              "fresh"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "question"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "answer_check",
      "description": "Record a clear SPOKEN answer to the waiting question: its sceneId, the index of the choice the child meant, and their actual words. The model scores it. Never use it for an unclear reply, a guess at what they meant, or an answer you supplied.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "sceneId": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "choice": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "maximum": 11
          },
          "words": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 650
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "sceneId",
          "choice",
          "words"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "leave_activity",
      "description": "Leave unfinished work when the child chooses something else or asks to move on. Earlier attempts are kept; no answer is invented.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {},
        "required": [],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "resume_activity",
      "description": "Give the work back to the child after help, exactly as it was, or reopen an answered question for another try. Either is recorded as helped.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {},
        "required": [],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    }
  ],
